$EXTERN Prout;

* Variable indices are case-insensitive: `e.X` and `e.x` denote the same Refal
* object (reference 1.3). The same holds for repeated-variable equality, so
* `s.A s.a` constrains both positions to the same symbol.
$ENTRY Go {
  (e.Text) = <Prout e.text> <Pair 'q' 'q'>;
}

Pair {
  s.A s.a = <Prout 'repeated variable folded case'>;
  e.Other = <Prout 'repeated variable did not fold case'>;
}
